#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:316
msgid "Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:317
msgid "Here are a few hints when working on the bytecode interpreter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:319
msgid ""
"Setting a breakpoint on ``CCEDiag`` and ``FFDiag`` will stop the debugger "
"when a diagnostic is emitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:321
msgid ""
"If you want to see the bytecode of a function call ``dump()`` on the "
"``interp::Function``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:322
msgid ""
"Additionally to the last point, ``interp::Function::dump(CodePtr)`` exists, "
"which you can pass the current ``OpPC`` and it will then show you where in "
"the bytecode that opcode is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:324
msgid ""
"``interp::Pointer`` has an ``operator<<`` that prints useful information. "
"Try it e.g. via ``llvm::errs() << Ptr << '\\n';``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:326
msgid "Printing ``APValue`` instances also works via ``APValue::dump()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.rst:327
msgid ""
"If you want to see *everything* that's being evaluated, add debugging output "
"to the ``evaluate*`` functions in ``Context.cpp``."
msgstr ""
